<title>USA: Raytheon unit wins $40.8 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Raytheon unit wins $40.8 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>GREENVILLE, Texas 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Raytheon E-Systems said on Wednesday it won a $40.8 million contract from the U.S. Air Force to build decoy-target systems to protect jet aircraft.</p>
<p>The contract includes four multi-year options which if exercised would bring its total value to $493 million.</p>
<p>Raytheon E-Systems is a unit of Raytheon Co of Lexington, Mass.</p>
<p>The contract calls for Raytheon to build more than 1,000 decoys as well as related products at its Goleta, Calif., plant. The decoys would protect F-16 fighters by luring guided missiles away from the aircraft.</p>
